parameters.jsonBody:
={{ JSON.stringify({
  model: $env['AI_MODEL_VALUATION_' + $env.AI_PROVIDER],
  max_tokens: 3500,
  temperature: 0.1,
  messages: [
    {
      role: "system",
      content: "You are a professional resale market analyst with deep expertise in pricing secondhand items across eBay, Facebook Marketplace, Craigslist, OfferUp, and other platforms. You analyze real market data to provide precise, realistic valuations and actionable pricing strategies. Your recommendations directly impact a seller's income — be accurate and conservative. Never guess; use the data provided. When citing a comparable item's URL, copy it EXACTLY from the data provided below -- never invent, guess, or construct a URL. Always respond in raw, valid JSON only."
    },
    {
      role: "user",
      content: `Analyze the following data and provide a complete valuation for this resale item.

PRODUCT PROFILE:
${JSON.stringify($('Parse Product Research').item.json)}

SELLER CONDITION: ${$('Set Variables').item.json.seller_condition}
MISSING ITEMS: ${$('Set Variables').item.json.missing_items}
SELLER-PROVIDED ORIGINAL PRICE: ${$('Set Variables').item.json.original_price || 'Not provided'}
SELLER-PROVIDED COMPARABLE LISTING: ${$('Set Variables').item.json.seller_comparable_url || 'Not provided'}${$('Set Variables').item.json.seller_comparable_url ? '\n' + (($('Fetch Seller Comparable').item.json.data || '').toString().slice(0, 3000)) : ''}

MARKET RESEARCH — eBay Sold/Active (web):
${$('Brave Search 4: eBay Sold Prices').item.json.web?.results?.slice(0,6).map(r => '• ' + r.title + '\n  ' + r.description + '\n  URL: ' + r.url).join('\n\n') ?? 'No results'}

MARKET RESEARCH — Used Market (FB, Craigslist, OfferUp):
${$('Brave Search 5: Used Market Prices').item.json.web?.results?.slice(0,6).map(r => '• ' + r.title + '\n  ' + r.description + '\n  URL: ' + r.url).join('\n\n') ?? 'No results'}

MARKET RESEARCH — Price Guides:
${$('Brave Search 6: Price Guide / Resale Value').item.json.web?.results?.slice(0,4).map(r => '• ' + r.title + '\n  ' + r.description + '\n  URL: ' + r.url).join('\n\n') ?? 'No results'}

EBAY API LIVE DATA:
${$('eBay: Browse API Search').item.json.itemSummaries?.slice(0,10).map(i => '• ' + i.title + ' — $' + i.price?.value + ' — ' + i.condition + '\n  URL: ' + i.itemWebUrl).join('\n') ?? 'eBay API not available'}

SCARCITY CHECK: If the product profile above indicates this item is discontinued, a convention/event exclusive, or a limited/numbered edition, apply a scarcity premium rather than depreciating from a \"new\" price the way you would for a mass-market item still in production — in that case, prioritize the eBay API live data and used-market search results over an uncertain retail/current-new price.

COMPARABLES -- LIKE ITEMS, NOT JUST EXACT MATCHES: For niche or rare items, an identical-title match often will not exist in the data above. Do not treat that as \"no data\" -- instead look for items that are SIMILAR: same franchise/brand line, same general product type (e.g. another framed convention-exclusive art print, another discontinued collectible from the same maker), comparable size/format, or comparable scarcity profile. A similar item is meaningfully better evidence than no item, but weight it accordingly: cap data_confidence at \"medium\" (never \"high\") when your strongest comparables are similar rather than exact matches, and say so in data_confidence_reason and in each comparable's note.

RETAIL PRICE FROM RESEARCH: $${$('Parse Product Research').item.json.retail_price_usd ?? 'Unknown'}
CURRENT NEW PRICE: $${$('Parse Product Research').item.json.current_new_price_usd ?? 'Unknown'}

ORIGINAL PRICE RULE: If a SELLER-PROVIDED ORIGINAL PRICE is given above, treat it as ground truth for original_retail_price_usd — sellers usually have a receipt or a clear memory of what they paid, which is more reliable than a price inferred from search results. Use it directly unless it is wildly implausible for the identified product (e.g. off by 10x). Only fall back to the research-derived retail price above when no seller-provided price was given.

Return ONLY this exact JSON:
{
  "original_retail_price_usd": "number or null",
  "current_new_price_usd": "number or null",
  "market_value_used_usd": "number — fair used market value for THIS condition",
  "ebay_sold_price_avg_usd": "number or null — average of recent eBay sold prices for similar condition",
  "ebay_active_price_avg_usd": "number or null — average of current eBay active listings",
  "facebook_marketplace_avg_usd": "number or null",
  "price_sell_fast_usd": "number — price to sell within 1-3 days (aggressive but not giving it away)",
  "price_maximize_profit_usd": "number — highest realistic price; may take 2-4 weeks",
  "recommended_price_usd": "number — your recommended sweet spot (sells within ~1 week)",
  "price_range_low_usd": "number — absolute floor (still fair)",
  "price_range_high_usd": "number — ceiling (optimistic but not unrealistic)",
  "condition_impact": "How the seller condition and missing items affect value versus a complete Like New example. 1-2 sentences.",
  "pricing_rationale": "2-3 sentences explaining the recommended price and the market factors driving it.",
  "sell_fast_strategy": "1-2 sentences: how to price and present this item to sell within 2-3 days.",
  "maximize_profit_strategy": "1-2 sentences: how to hold out for maximum value (timing, platform, framing).",
  "best_platform_to_sell": "eBay | Facebook Marketplace | Both | OfferUp | Other",
  "best_platform_reason": "Why this platform maximizes value or speed for this specific item.",
  "data_confidence": "high | medium | low",
  "data_confidence_reason": "One sentence explaining confidence in the valuation data.",
  "comparables": [
    {
      "title": "The comparable item's title/name, copied from the data above",
      "price_usd": "number or null",
      "url": "The EXACT url copied from the data above (eBay API URL, a Brave search result URL, or the seller-provided comparable URL) -- null if no real url is available. NEVER invent one.",
      "platform": "eBay | Facebook Marketplace | Other",
      "match_type": "exact | similar | seller_provided -- exact means same product/edition/format; similar means related but not identical (see COMPARABLES guidance above)",
      "note": "Short note on why this is a comparable and how much weight it carries"
    }
  ]
}

List up to 5 comparables, most relevant first. Prefer exact matches; include similar items when exact ones are not available. If a SELLER-PROVIDED COMPARABLE LISTING was given above, include it as one entry with match_type "seller_provided" using its url and any price you can determine from the fetched page content. If there is truly no usable comparable data anywhere above, return an empty array -- do not fabricate entries.`
    }
  ]
}) }}

